COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[354,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nDonate to a charitable organization that helps youth to get married.\nAsk Allah to guide you to His light.\nRead the daily morning and evening remembrance of Allah (Athkar) while inside a mosque.\nguid\nPoverty is not an obstacle to getting married, rather, it may be a cause for becoming rich.\nEnsure to know the narrations in the Quran, as they contain signs, lessons and admonitions.\nBeing guided to the light of Allah is a cause for enlightened intuition. In this Surah, Allah explains the causes for this light, its places and obstacles.\nrefl\nوَأَنكِحُواْ ٱلۡأَيَٰمَىٰ مِنكُمۡ وَٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ مِنۡ عِبَادِكُمۡ وَإِمَآئِكُمۡۚ إِن يَكُونُواْ فُقَرَآءَ يُغۡنِهِمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ وَٰسِعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٣٢\nThe commands to maintain chastity are followed by guiding the believers to what helps keep their souls chaste and their gazes low. Allah directs the guardians to arrange marriages for their female slaves, and not leave them infatuated with others, since marriage keeps both women and men chaste. Ibn Ashur: 18/215.\nWhen the Quran commands to maintain low gazing and chastity, it indicates some of means to help the believers do that. How does this verse indicate that?\nوَأَنكِحُواْ ٱلۡأَيَٰمَىٰ مِنكُمۡ وَٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ مِنۡ عِبَادِكُمۡ وَإِمَآئِكُمۡۚ إِن يَكُونُواْ فُقَرَآءَ يُغۡنِهِمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ وَٰسِعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٣٢\nSince man has a natural disposition to worry about the lack of provision, Allah answers, as if saying: Man may be incapable of marriage due to his poverty, saying: (If they should be poor, Allah will enrich them) when they get married (from His bounty), because He decreed for every soul its provision, hence, do not let their poor status prevent you from arranging their marriage. Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq (t) said: \"Obey Allah in what He commands you of marriage, He will fulfill to you what He promised you of enrichment.\" Al-Biqai: 13/265.\nThis verse indicates one of the reasons to become rich. What is it?\nوَلۡيَسۡتَعۡفِفِ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَجِدُونَ نِكَاحًا حَتَّىٰ يُغۡنِيَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦۗ\nThis is guidance to those who are eager for marriage but do not possess the means to pursue it to do what is best for them, which is keeping themselves chaste. Al-Alusi: 9/344.\nWhat should be our advice to a single person? What is Allah's promise to him?\nوَلۡيَسۡتَعۡفِفِ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَجِدُونَ نِكَاحًا حَتَّىٰ يُغۡنِيَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦۗ\nThis is a command to keep oneself chaste. The Arabic word used indicates striving to keep oneself chaste when one does not have the means for it. (Cannot afford marriage), they cannot get married for any reason. Ibn Juzay: 2/91.\nFor one who does not have the means to get married, what should he do?\nٱللَّهُ نُورُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ نُّورٌ عَلَىٰ نُورٖۚ يَهۡدِي ٱللَّهُ لِنُورِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُۚ\nAfter the verses about lowering the gaze, Allah mentions the verse of the light, and says, (Allah is the Light of the heavens and earth). Shah bin Shuja Al-Karmani had an impeccable intuition, and he used to say: \"He who followed Sunnah, feared Allah, lowered his gaze toward forbidden things, refrained from following his desires, and consumed only lawful food, his intuition would never be wrong.\" Allah's reward befits the servant's deed, so when he lowers his gaze toward what Allah prohibited, Allah compensates him with something suitable and better, which is enlightening his insight and inspiring him. Ibn Taimyah: 4/513.\nThe verse of the light comes after verses about lowering the gaze, why?\nنُّورٌ عَلَىٰ نُورٖۚ يَهۡدِي ٱللَّهُ لِنُورِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُۚ\n(Light upon light), some of the righteous predecessors said: This is about the believer who speaks with wisdom, even though he did not hear it before, and when he hears it, it becomes light upon light; the light of faith in his heart matches the light of the Quran. Ibn Taimyah: 4/513.\nWhen does the believer have two lights?\nفِي بُيُوتٍ أَذِنَ ٱللَّهُ أَن تُرۡفَعَ وَيُذۡكَرَ فِيهَا ٱسۡمُهُۥ يُسَبِّحُ لَهُۥ فِيهَا بِٱلۡغُدُوِّ وَٱلۡأٓصَالِ ٣٦\n(Exalting), praying and glorifying. (Him), to Allah alone. (Within them in the morning), early morning prayer [Al-Fajr]. (And the evenings), prayers at the latter part of the day, so they begin and end their day with Allah's remembrance, thus, they will be protected in between, and their works will be blessed. Al-Biqai: 13/278.\nWhat is the benefit for a Muslim to begin and end his day with prayer and remembrance of Allah?\nwords\nالأَيَامَىUnmarried persons\nوَإِمَائِكُمFemale slaves\nالبِغَاءِProstitution\nتَحَصُّنًاChastity\nكَمِشكَاةٍA niche\nدُرِّيٌّShining"],[355,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nWhen you hear the call for prayer, leave your distractions and keep up with the first Takbir of the prayer.\nAsk only Allah to enlighten and guide you, for He is the only One Who can do that.\nSay, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He, Glorified is Allah the Great\" as many as a hundred times.\nguid\nFearing Allah in worldly life is a cause for being safe on the Day of Resurrection.\nThe disbelievers' deeds in worldly life will be a total loss in the Hereafter.\nSupplicate Allah when it rains, for supplication is answered then.\nrefl\nرِجَالٞ لَّا تُلۡهِيهِمۡ تِجَٰرَةٞ وَلَا بَيۡعٌ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ\n(Are men), is indicative of their high drives, good intentions and firm resolves by which they became attached to the mosques that are the house of Allah on His earth, and places for worshiping Him, thanking Him, believing in His Oneness and exalting Him. Ibn Kathir: 3/284.\nAllah describes those who are attached to the mosques as (men). What is indication of that?\nرِجَالٞ لَّا تُلۡهِيهِمۡ تِجَٰرَةٞ وَلَا بَيۡعٌ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ وَإِقَامِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَإِيتَآءِ ٱلزَّكَوٰةِ\nMany of the Prophet's (ﷺ) Companions said: \"This verse was revealed about the traders in the market, who when they heard the call for prayer, they left all distractions and hastened to prayer.\" When Salem bin Abdullah saw the traders coming to the prayer, he said: \"These are whom Allah meant when He said: (Neither commerce nor sale distracts from the remembrance of Allah)”. Al-Qurtubi: 15/286.\nWhat are the traits of men whom Allah praised in this verse?\nرِجَالٞ لَّا تُلۡهِيهِمۡ تِجَٰرَةٞ وَلَا بَيۡعٌ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ وَإِقَامِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَإِيتَآءِ ٱلزَّكَوٰةِ يَخَافُونَ يَوۡمٗا تَتَقَلَّبُ فِيهِ ٱلۡقُلُوبُ وَٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ ٣٧\nBecause forsaking worldly matters is very hard for most people, and the love of earning by means of various kinds of trade is dear to them; giving it up is very hard for most of them, and it may not come naturally to them to give precedence to the rights of Allah over that. Allah mentions what will motivate them to do it by means of encouragement and warnings, (They fear a Day in which the hearts and eyes will [fearfully] turn about). Al-Saadi: 569.\nThe verse ends with (They fear a Day in which the hearts and eyes will turn about). Why?\nلِيَجۡزِيَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ أَحۡسَنَ مَا عَمِلُواْ وَيَزِيدَهُم مِّن فَضۡلِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَرۡزُقُ مَن يَشَآءُ بِغَيۡرِ حِسَابٖ ٣٨\nAllah mentions the reward on good deeds, and did not mention the recompense on the bad deeds -even though he will recompense for them- for two reasons: First: This is meant to be an encouragement. Second: It is a description of people who do not commit major sins, and thus, their minor ones are forgiven. Al-Qurtubi: 15/304.\nAllah mentions the reward for good deeds without mentioning of misdeeds. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَعۡمَٰلُهُمۡ كَسَرَابِۢ بِقِيعَةٖ يَحۡسَبُهُ ٱلظَّمۡـَٔانُ مَآءً حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءَهُۥ لَمۡ يَجِدۡهُ شَيۡـٔٗا\nThe disbeliever thinks that he is doing something good, and that he has achieved something, but when Allah judges him on the Day of Resurrection, and brings him to account and examines his deeds, he will find that nothing has been accepted at all, either because of a lack of sincere belief, or because he did not follow the proper ways of Sharia, as Allah says, (We will turn to whatever deeds they did and turn them into scattered dust). [25:23]. Ibn Kathir: 3/286.\nWhat will be the reason for rejecting deeds on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَعۡمَٰلُهُمۡ كَسَرَابِۢ بِقِيعَةٖ يَحۡسَبُهُ ٱلظَّمۡـَٔانُ مَآءً حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءَهُۥ لَمۡ يَجِدۡهُ شَيۡـٔٗا\nAfter mentioning the believers, Allah presents two examples of the disbelievers' deeds, the first describes the status of their deeds in the Hereafter, and that they will not benefit from them. In fact, their reward will fade away like a mirage, which is the appearance of a sheet of running water on the ground due to sun light during midday time. Ibn Juzay: 2/94.\nThe polytheists perform many acts of worship but with shirk. How will their deeds be judged on the Day of Resurrection?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُسَبِّحُ لَهُۥ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلطَّيۡرُ صَٰٓفَّٰتٖۖ كُلّٞ قَدۡ عَلِمَ صَلَاتَهُۥ وَتَسۡبِيحَهُۥۗ\nAmong all creatures, the birds are singled out for mention because they are between heavens and earth, thus, they are outside the rules that govern both. Al-Qurtubi: 15/306.\nAfter mentioning heavens and earth, Allah mentions the birds. Why?\nwords\nكَسَرَابٍLike a mirage\nبِقِيعَةٍA lowland\nلُجِّيٍّDeep\nيَغشَاهُCovered\nصَآفَّاتٍWith wings outspread\nيُزجِيHe drives"],[356,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nReflect on the diversity of Allah's creation, then praise Him for shaping and refining your creation.\nAsk only Allah to guide you to His straight path.\nShare a message about the risk of objecting to the rules of Allah, and that it is a trait of hypocrites.\nguid\nThose who possess acute insight and enlightened minds are admonished by the signs of Allah in the universe.\nSubmission to Sharia must be in all cases, whether the its ruling is in your favor or not.\nThose who fear Allah and obey Him and His Messenger (ﷺ) are the triumphant, because they will enter Paradise and be saved from Hellfire.\nrefl\nيُقَلِّبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّيۡلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَعِبۡرَةٗ لِّأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرِ ٤٤\nMeaning: A lesson to those with insight who reflect and become aware. The word (vision) here means insight. It is also said that it means a clear vision. The word (vision) is used instead of \"insight\" because the intended meaning is clear. Al-Alusi: 9/384.\nWhy is the word (vision) used instead of \"insight\"?\nلَّقَدۡ أَنزَلۡنَآ ءَايَٰتٖ مُّبَيِّنَٰتٖۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَهۡدِي مَن يَشَآءُ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٤٦\n(Distinct verses): This includes all signs created by Allah for people to reflect upon, and all verses in His Book that alert and remind them. Ibn Atiyah: 4/191.\nWhat are the verses by which Allah guides the believers?\nوَيَقُولُونَ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَبِٱلرَّسُولِ وَأَطَعۡنَا ثُمَّ يَتَوَلَّىٰ فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ ذَٰلِكَۚ وَمَآ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ بِٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٤٧\nThese verses indicate that faith is not just words, unless those words are accompanied by action. Therefore, the one who turns away from obedience has no faith. Al-Saadi: 572.\nThis verse contains an important point with regard to faith in Allah. What is it?\nوَإِذَا دُعُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ لِيَحۡكُمَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ إِذَا فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٤٨\nIt is said that a hypocrite whose name was Bishr was involved in a dispute with a Jew who called on him to go to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) to judge between them, but the hypocrite refused, and suggested they go to Ka'b Bin Al-Ashraf, hence this verse was revealed. Az-Zahrawi narrated that Alhasan bin Abi Alhasan said: \"Whoever is called by his opponent to a Muslim judge, but refuses, is wrongful.\" Ibn Atiyah: 4/191.\nWhat should be the stand of the believer when called to be judged by Sharia law?\nأَمۡ يَخَافُونَ أَن يَحِيفَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَرَسُولُهُۥۚ\nIt is forbidden to think negatively of the rulings of Sharia or to think that they are contrary to justice and wisdom. Al-Saadi: 572.\nSatisfaction with Sharia laws is a blessing from Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَن يُطِعِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَيَخۡشَ ٱللَّهَ وَيَتَّقۡهِ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡفَآئِزُونَ ٥٢\nThis verse combines the causes of triumph in the Hereafter, as well as those in worldly life. Ibn Ashur: 18/276.\nThis verse has concise words with comprehensive meaning. Explain.\nوَأَقۡسَمُواْ بِٱللَّهِ جَهۡدَ أَيۡمَٰنِهِمۡ لَئِنۡ أَمَرۡتَهُمۡ لَيَخۡرُجُنَّۖ قُل لَّا تُقۡسِمُواْۖ طَاعَةٞ مَّعۡرُوفَةٌۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ خَبِيرُۢ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ ٥٣\nThe hypocrites said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \"Wherever you are, we will be; if you go, we will go; if you stay, we will stay; and if you command us to fight, we will.\" Thus, Allah says, (Say, \"Do not swear\"), do not take an oath, as talking is done. ([Such] obedience is known), which means that this is obedience with words only without faith, and your lies are known, because you say what you do not do. Al-Baghawi: 3/309.\nDo words suffice without faith of the heart?\nwords\nمُذعِنِينَThey are submissive\nمَرَضٌHypocrisy\nارتَابُواThey have doubt\nيَحِيفَUnjust\nجَهدَ أَيمَانِهِمTheir strongest oath"],[357,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nPerform the five daily prayers humbly and in congregation, because that is establishing the prayer.\nGive some of your money to charity.\nStudy, with those around you, some etiquettes of asking for permission.\nguid\nAdhering to the Quranic verses and authentic Prophetic Hadiths leads to contentment in this life and in the Hereafter while turning away from them leads to misguidance and loss.\nAllah's promise of giving authority in the land and succession is contingent on worshiping Him and abandoning shirk.\nCompare between a contemporary powerful disbelieving nation to an ancient powerful one that was destroyed by Allah.\nrefl\nقُلۡ أَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُواْ ٱلرَّسُولَۖ فَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَإِنَّمَا عَلَيۡهِ مَا حُمِّلَ وَعَلَيۡكُم مَّا حُمِّلۡتُمۡۖ وَإِن تُطِيعُوهُ تَهۡتَدُواْۚ وَمَا عَلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ إِلَّا ٱلۡبَلَٰغُ ٱلۡمُبِينُ ٥٤\n(And if you obey him, you will be guided), this statement encourages obedience, and it follows the intimidation implied in this statement (and you are responsible for your duty). Ibn Ashur: 18/281.\nThis verse combines encouragement and intimidation. Explain.\nقُلۡ أَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُواْ ٱلرَّسُولَۖ فَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَإِنَّمَا عَلَيۡهِ مَا حُمِّلَ وَعَلَيۡكُم مَّا حُمِّلۡتُمۡۖ وَإِن تُطِيعُوهُ تَهۡتَدُواْۚ وَمَا عَلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ إِلَّا ٱلۡبَلَٰغُ ٱلۡمُبِينُ ٥٤\n(And if you obey him, you will be guided) to the straight path in word and deed, but there is no way for you to be guided except through obedience; without which guidance is not possible for you, in fact, it is impossible. Al-Saadi: 573.\nIs there a way to guidance other than obeying the Messenger (ﷺ)?\nوَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مِنكُمۡ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَيَسۡتَخۡلِفَنَّهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ كَمَا ٱسۡتَخۡلَفَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡ وَلَيُمَكِّنَنَّ لَهُمۡ دِينَهُمُ ٱلَّذِي ٱرۡتَضَىٰ لَهُمۡ وَلَيُبَدِّلَنَّهُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ خَوۡفِهِمۡ أَمۡنٗاۚ\nThis verse is a clear proof that Muslim Caliphs such as Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman, Ali, Alhasan, and Mu'awiya were pleasing to Allah because He extensively made them successors, as He made those who came before them, helped them to conquer the land from east to west, and made Persian kings and Roman Caesars frightened of them. Ibn Ashur: 18/286.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of these Companions (j). How?\nوَمَن كَفَرَ بَعۡدَ ذَٰلِكَ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡفَٰسِقُونَ ٥٥\n(But whoever disbelieves after that), after you have been given full power and authority, O Muslims (then those are the defiantly disobedient) who have drifted away from obedience to Allah, and have become corrupt, thus, they are no longer righteous people and are no longer qualified for anything good, because if a person gives up faith when the religion is prevailing, its enemies have been defeated, and there are no impediments to faith, this is indicative of his corrupt intentions and evil nature, since there is no reason for him to abandon faith except that. Al-Saadi: 573.\nAllah describes those who disbelieve after being given authority as defiantly disobedient. Why?\nوَأَقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتُواْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَأَطِيعُواْ ٱلرَّسُولَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُرۡحَمُونَ ٥٦\nHere, Allah enjoins establishing prayer and the giving zakah. These two are the greatest and most virtuous acts of worship, which combine the fulfillment of duties toward Allah and toward His creation, in which the individual shows devotion to Allah and shows kindness to people. That is followed by a general command (and obey the Messenger)...(so that) if you do this, (you may receive mercy). Whoever seeks mercy, this is the way to attain it. Whoever hopes to find mercy without establishing prayer, giving zakah and obeying the Messenger (ﷺ), is indulging in wishful thinking and is lying, as his soul makes him feel content with false hopes. Al-Saadi: 573.\nAmong all ordinances that require obedience to the Messenger, prayer and zakah are singled out for mention. Why? What do you think of one who hopes for Allah's mercy, but disobeys the Messenger and falls short in his prayer and zakah?\nلَا تَحۡسَبَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مُعۡجِزِينَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ وَمَأۡوَىٰهُمُ ٱلنَّارُۖ وَلَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ٥٧\n(In the land), this includes all parts of the earth, which means: Do not think that they would escape Allah's punishment at any part of the earth, no matter where they go. Al-Alusi: 9/398.\nIn this verse, what does this term, (in the land) indicate?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لِيَسۡتَـٔۡذِنكُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ مَلَكَتۡ أَيۡمَٰنُكُمۡ وَٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يَبۡلُغُواْ ٱلۡحُلُمَ مِنكُمۡ ثَلَٰثَ مَرَّٰتٖۚ\nThese particular times are specified because they are when people are resting alone, and putting aside their clothing, thus, they are exposed and do not wish for anyone to see them. Al-Qurtubi: 15/313.\nThese times are specified for which permission is required. Why?\nwords\nعَلَيهِ مَا حُمِّلَHe is responsible for conveying the message\nوَعَلَيكُم مَا حُمِّلتُمYou are responsible for your duties\nمُعجِزِينَEscaping from punishment\nجُنَاحٌA blame"],[358,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nAsk permission before entering upon your brothers and sisters.\nRemind women who are close to you of wearing hijab, guarding their chastity, and maintaining dignity.\nWhen entering your house, say, \"In the Name of Allah\", then greet others.\nguid\nNotice how Sharia eliminates the likelihood of trials, and blocks the means to corruption. This great knowledge is essential for all of us.\nReflect on the ease of Sharia and its alleviation to people, specially the excused persons among them.\nWhen greeting people, always use the greeting ordained by Allah: \"Peace and Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.\"\nrefl\nوَٱلۡقَوَٰعِدُ مِنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ ٱلَّٰتِي لَا يَرۡجُونَ نِكَاحٗا فَلَيۡسَ عَلَيۡهِنَّ جُنَاحٌ أَن يَضَعۡنَ ثِيَابَهُنَّ غَيۡرَ مُتَبَرِّجَٰتِۢ بِزِينَةٖۖ وَأَن يَسۡتَعۡفِفۡنَ خَيۡرٞ لَّهُنَّۗ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٦٠\nElderly women are singled out for this ruling because of the normal disinterest of men in them, thus, they are allowed what other women are not in order to ease this difficulty for them. Al-Qurtubi: 15/340.\nAllah singles out elderly women for this ruling, why? What is inferred from this verse for other women?\nوَلَا عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِكُمۡ أَن تَأۡكُلُواْ مِنۢ بُيُوتِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ ءَابَآئِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ أُمَّهَٰتِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ إِخۡوَٰنِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ أَخَوَٰتِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ أَعۡمَٰمِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ عَمَّٰتِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ أَخۡوَٰلِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ خَٰلَٰتِكُمۡ أَوۡ مَا مَلَكۡتُم مَّفَاتِحَهُۥٓ أَوۡ صَدِيقِكُمۡۚ\nThe statement that there is no blame for eating from these houses applies to cases where that is done without express permission. The wisdom behind it is known from the context, since the custom with regard to the people mentioned here is usually to tolerate a person's eating from their houses, because of kinship ties, complete authority or close friendship. But if it is known that a person does not allow that or is stingy with regard to food, then it is not permissible to eat from his house, and blame is not lifted in that case. Al-Saadi: 575.\nIf one of those mentioned in the verse does not allow eating from his house, what is the ruling in this case?\nوَلَا عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِكُمۡ أَن تَأۡكُلُواْ مِنۢ بُيُوتِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ ءَابَآئِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ أُمَّهَٰتِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ إِخۡوَٰنِكُمۡ أَوۡ بُيُوتِ أَخَوَٰتِكُمۡ\nAllah mentions houses of relatives, but not the son's. The Quran interpreters said: \"That is because the son's house is included in (your houses) since a son's house is his father's.\" Al-Qurtubi: 15/347.\nHouses of relatives are mentioned, but not the son's. Why?\nأَوۡ صَدِيقِكُمۡۚ\nIn this verse, Allah combines friends with close relatives, because affection brings people together. In the book of An-Naqqash, Ibn Abbas (k) said: \"A friend is a confidant more so than a relative; do you not see how the dwellers of Hellfire appeal for help: (So now we have no intercessors ` nor a close friend)\" [26:100-101]. Al-Qurtubi: 15/351.\nAllah combines friends with relatives. Why?\nلَيۡسَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَأۡكُلُواْ جَمِيعًا أَوۡ أَشۡتَاتٗاۚ\nThis verse says that there is no blame, but that does not mean that eating separately is better, because it is preferable to eat together. Al-Saadi: 575\nWhich is better: Eating together or alone?\nفَسَلِّمُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِكُمۡ\nMeaning: Greet one another. This indicates that all Muslims resemble one body in their mutual kindness, compassion and sympathy. Al-Saadi: 575.\nIn this verse, what does this term (yourselves) indicate?\nفَإِذَا دَخَلۡتُم بُيُوتٗا فَسَلِّمُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِكُمۡ تَحِيَّةٗ مِّنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ مُبَٰرَكَةٗ طَيِّبَةٗۚ\nGreetings is described as (blessed) because it contains supplication, and draws affection to the greeter. Ibn Atiyah: 4/197.\nGreetings is described as (blessed), why?\nwords\nوَالقَوَاعِدُElderly women of post-menstrual age\nمُتَبَرِّجَاتٍDisplaying their hidden adornment\nمَا مَلَكتُم مَفَاتِحَهُHouses with which you are entrusted to keep\nأَشتَاتًاEating separately"],[359,"§An-Nur, Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nSeek Allah's forgiveness for all Muslims, all believers, the living and the deceased.\nInvoke Allah's blessings upon the Prophet (ﷺ) every time his name comes up.\nShare a message in which you explain the risk of dissent from the Prophet's (ﷺ) guidance.\nguid\nRevering Allah's Messenger (ﷺ), and prohibiting impoliteness to him during his lifetime and after his death is a duty of all Muslims.\nWhoever is defiant to the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) is at the risk of facing an evil end of life; we seek refuge with Allah from that.\nAllah will inform you of what you did, the minor and the major, therefore, ensure to hear from Him that which will please you.\nrefl\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَإِذَا كَانُواْ مَعَهُۥ عَلَىٰٓ أَمۡرٖ جَامِعٖ لَّمۡ يَذۡهَبُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَسۡتَـٔۡذِنُوهُۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَـٔۡذِنُونَكَ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦۚ\n(On a public matter), a matter that gathers them all, such as an eminent war, a congregational prayer or a consultation on an urgent matter. (They do not leave), they do not depart from what brought them together until they ask permission from Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). Al-Tabari: 19/228.\nAsking permission indicates faith and ensures the success of the collective efforts. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡ لَهُمُ ٱللَّهَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٦٢\n(And ask Allah's forgiveness for them), supplicate Allah to favor them by forgiving their sins. (Allah is All-Forgiving) of His repentant servants' sins. (Most Merciful) toward them, Who does not punish them for sins after which they repented. Al-Tabari: 19/229.\nSupplicating Allah for those who are under his command in their absence, is the sign of the leader's forbearance and success. Explain.\nلَّا تَجۡعَلُواْ دُعَآءَ ٱلرَّسُولِ بَيۡنَكُمۡ كَدُعَآءِ بَعۡضِكُم بَعۡضٗاۚ\nThey are forbidden from calling the Messenger (ﷺ) as they do with each other, either by words or in any condition. As for words, they should not say: O Muhammad, O son of Abdullah, or, O son of Abdul Muttalib, but they should say: O Messenger of Allah, O Prophet of Allah, or, O Aba Al-Qasim. As for the proper condition, they should not call him from behind walls, and should not be persistent if he does not come to them. Ibn Ashur: 18/309.\nVenerating Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) is part of venerating Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nلَّا تَجۡعَلُواْ دُعَآءَ ٱلرَّسُولِ بَيۡنَكُمۡ كَدُعَآءِ بَعۡضِكُم بَعۡضٗاۚ\nThis command emphasizes the veneration of the Messenger (ﷺ). It is said that a scholar among his people is like a Prophet among his Ummah (nation), hence, he should be respected when addressed and given a special attention. Al-Alusi: 9/419.\nThere are beautiful etiquettes that a student of Islamic knowledge should observe with his teacher and other scholars. Explain in light of this verse.\nتَبَارَكَ ٱلَّذِي نَزَّلَ ٱلۡفُرۡقَانَ عَلَىٰ عَبۡدِهِۦ لِيَكُونَ لِلۡعَٰلَمِينَ نَذِيرًا ١\nThere are two explanations for calling the Quran: The Criterion. First: It differentiates between truth and falsehood, and the believer and disbeliever. Second: It clarifies what is lawful and what is unlawful. Al-Qurtubi: 15/366.\nThe Quran is called: (The Criterion). Why?\nتَبَارَكَ ٱلَّذِي نَزَّلَ ٱلۡفُرۡقَانَ عَلَىٰ عَبۡدِهِۦ لِيَكُونَ لِلۡعَٰلَمِينَ نَذِيرًا ١\n(His slave), our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ), and referring to him as (slave) is honoring him, proclaiming that he is at the highest levels of submission to Allah, and alerting to the fact that a messenger can only be a slave to the sender, which is a response to Christians. Al-Alusi: 9/422.\nIn sending down the Quran, Allah refers to the status of \"submission\" rather than status of Prophethood and Message. What do you learn from that?\nوَخَلَقَ كُلَّ شَيۡءٖ فَقَدَّرَهُۥ تَقۡدِيرٗا ٢\nAllah shaped and enabled everything for what suits its livelihood, without flaws or imperfection. It is said: He predestined an appointed time and a provision for everything; thus, it is destined to happen. Al-Baghawi: 3/321.\nShow an aspect of Allah's greatness in determining His creation.\nwords\nأَمرٍ جَامِعٍA public matter of interest to Muslims\nدُعَاءَ الرَّسُولِCalling the Prophet: O Messenger of Allah, not: O Muhammad\nيَتَسَلَّلُونَ مِنكُمThose of you who slip away without permission\nلِوَاذًاLeaving by hiding behind others\nفِتنَةٌAn affliction, hardship, punishment\nفَقَدَّرَهُHe shaped it for what suits its livelihood"],[360,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, grant me a good outcome on all of my affairs, and save me from disgrace in this world, and punishment in the Hereafter.\"\nGive a talk or share a message about the Oneness of Allah, conveying to people that the owner of all affairs of His servants is Allah. No Benefactor or Afflicter except Him.\nAsk Allah for forgiveness and mercy.\nguid\nRemember that Allah knows what is concealed, let alone what is revealed.\nMocking those who call others to Allah, and plotting against them, is a habit of the deniers.\nEndure patiently the harm in the cause of Allah, as the Messenger (ﷺ) endured great harm from people.\nrefl\nوَٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ ءَالِهَةٗ لَّا يَخۡلُقُونَ شَيۡٔٗا وَهُمۡ يُخۡلَقُونَ وَلَا يَمۡلِكُونَ لِأَنفُسِهِمۡ ضَرّٗا وَلَا نَفۡعٗا وَلَا يَمۡلِكُونَ مَوۡتٗا وَلَا حَيَوٰةٗ وَلَا نُشُورٗا ٣\nAllah, the Almighty, describes the gods of which the polytheists worship besides Him as having six traits. Each of these traits is conclusive proof that worshiping these gods besides Allah is baseless, rather, it is an absolute transgression and utter ignorance. First: They create nothing because they cannot. Second: They are all created by the One Who creates everything. Third: They do not possess for themselves any harm or benefit. Fourth, fifth, and sixth: They do not possess the power to cause death, life or resurrection. Al-Shanqiti: 6/9.\nWhat are the deficiencies of everything that is worshiped besides Allah?\nقُلۡ أَنزَلَهُ ٱلَّذِي يَعۡلَمُ ٱلسِّرَّ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ\nThe (secret) is mentioned here because He Who knows the secret, definitely knows what is declared. Al-Qurtubi: 15/369.\nThe (secret) is mentioned here without mentioning the declared. Why?\nوَقَالُوٓاْ أَسَٰطِيرُ ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٱكۡتَتَبَهَا فَهِيَ تُمۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِ بُكۡرَةٗ وَأَصِيلٗا ٥ قُلۡ أَنزَلَهُ ٱلَّذِي يَعۡلَمُ ٱلسِّرَّ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ٦\n(He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful), this is an invitation to them to repent and turn back to Allah, telling them that His mercy is vast and His patience is immense. Whoever repents to Him, He will accept his repentance. Despite all their lies, immorality, falsehood, disbelief, and stubbornness, and saying what they said about the Messenger and the Quran, Allah still invites them to repent and give up their sins, and to come to Islam and true guidance.Ibn Kathir: 3/299.\nThis verse ends with (He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful), why?\nقُلۡ أَنزَلَهُ ٱلَّذِي يَعۡلَمُ ٱلسِّرَّ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ٦\nIf it is said: How is this statement (He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful) relevant to what precedes it? The answer is: When Allah mentions the sayings of the disbelievers, He concludes the verse with that in order to show His forgiveness and mercy, in that He did not punish them swiftly, but gave them respite, and if they accept Islam, then He would accept their repentance and forgive them. Ibn Juzay: 2/103.\nWhat is the relevance of saying (He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful) to what precedes it?\nوَقَالُواْ مَالِ هَٰذَا ٱلرَّسُولِ يَأۡكُلُ ٱلطَّعَامَ وَيَمۡشِي فِي ٱلۡأَسۡوَاقِ\nThis verse is quoted as evidence by those who say that it is permitted for scholars, clergymen, and righteous people to enter the markets, contrary to those who disliked that for them. Al-Alusi: 9/427.\nModesty and mingling with people help the preacher in his cause. How can you infer this meaning from this verse?\nوَقَالُواْ مَالِ هَٰذَا ٱلرَّسُولِ يَأۡكُلُ ٱلطَّعَامَ وَيَمۡشِي فِي ٱلۡأَسۡوَاقِ\n(And they say, \"What is this messenger\"), they meant Muhammad (ﷺ). (Eats food) like we do. (And walks in the markets) he works for living like we do, so he cannot be distinguished by Prophethood. Moreover, they used to say to him: \"You are neither an angel nor a king because you eat while an angel does not; you are not a king because a king does not shop while you shop and bargain.\" All that which they said was invalid, since he eats because he is a human being, and he walks in the markets because he is modest, which is a trait of his that does not contradict Prophethood. Al-Baghawi: 3/322.\nSigns of the truthfulness of a preacher are being modest and realistic in his actions. Explain in light of this verse.\nبَلۡ كَذَّبُواْ بِٱلسَّاعَةِۖ\nMeaning: They say this in stubborn disbelief, not because they are seeking insight and guidance, rather, their disbelief in the Day of Resurrection makes them say what they say. Ibn Kathir: 3/300.\nWhat is the reason for most of what disbelievers and hypocrites say and do?\nwords\nنُشُورًاResurrection\nإِفكٌ افتَرَاهُA falsehood he invented\nوَزُورًاA hideous lie\nأَسَاطِيرُ الأوَّلِينَLegends of the former peoples\nسَعِيرًاA Blazing Fire"],[361,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness if you caused someone to deviate from the right path, or lured someone into wrongdoing, for you will be held accountable for it.\nAsk Allah to grant you the Garden of Eternity, and to guide you to be among His pious servants.\nSay, \"O Allah, changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nguid\nRighteousness is a virtue, so whoever believes and fears Allah deserves the highest of ranks.\nWhat a terrifying sight to witness on Judgment Day! When the worshiped will be questioned about those who worshiped them, and the oppressed about their oppressors.\nA long luxurious life can be risky to a person who is heedless of his Lord.\nrefl\nإِذَا رَأَتۡهُم مِّن مَّكَانِۢ بَعِيدٖ سَمِعُواْ لَهَا تَغَيُّظٗا وَزَفِيرٗا ١٢\nThe wrath of Hellfire against them stems from the wrath of its Creator, and its flames will increase because of the increase in their disbelief and evil. Al-Saadi: 579.\nWhy will the dwellers of Hellfire incur its wrath?\nوَإِذَآ أُلۡقُواْ مِنۡهَا مَكَانٗا ضَيِّقٗا مُّقَرَّنِينَ\nIt will be a combination of the tight and narrow space and the overcrowding of inhabitants, who will be bound together in chains and shackles. Al-Saadi: 579.\nThis verse presents different ways of tormenting the disbelievers. Explain.\nوَيَوۡمَ يَحۡشُرُهُمۡ وَمَا يَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَيَقُولُ ءَأَنتُمۡ أَضۡلَلۡتُمۡ عِبَادِي هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ أَمۡ هُمۡ ضَلُّواْ ٱلسَّبِيلَ ١٧\nIf someone asks: If these worshiped idols will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, how will they speak when they are only inanimate objects? The answer is: Allah will make them speak, just as He will make the hands and feet speak. Al-Qurtubi: 15/378.\nHow will the idols, which are inanimate objects, speak on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَيَوۡمَ يَحۡشُرُهُمۡ وَمَا يَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَيَقُولُ ءَأَنتُمۡ أَضۡلَلۡتُمۡ عِبَادِي هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ أَمۡ هُمۡ ضَلُّواْ ٱلسَّبِيلَ ١٧\nMeaning: Allah will say to the worshiped: (Did you mislead these servants of Mine, or did they stray) on their own and by their choice, and you did not? Even though Allah is well aware of them, however, this question is a rebuke to the disbelievers who worshiped them. Ibn Juzay: 2/104.\nAllah's question to the worshiped idols is a rebuke to the disbelievers. Explain.\nوَلَٰكِن مَّتَّعۡتَهُمۡ وَءَابَآءَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ نَسُواْ ٱلذِّكۡرَ وَكَانُواْ قَوۡمَۢا بُورٗا ١٨\n(Pleasures), means that You provided them in this worldly life with wealth, health, and longevity until after the death of the Messengers (p). (Until they forgot the message), means that they neglected Your remembrance, and ascribed partners to You, out of their insolence and ignorance. Al-Qurtubi: 15/379.\nExplain the risk of being fully distracted by diversion and enjoying life's pleasures.\nقَالُواْ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ مَا كَانَ يَنۢبَغِي لَنَآ أَن نَّتَّخِذَ مِن دُونِكَ مِنۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ وَلَٰكِن مَّتَّعۡتَهُمۡ وَءَابَآءَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ نَسُواْ ٱلذِّكۡرَ وَكَانُواْ قَوۡمَۢا بُورٗا ١٨\nThey said: (Glory be to You), they exalted Allah above having a partner. (It was not for us to take besides You any allies), We would never take your enemies as our allies, rather, You are our ally, not them. It is also said that it means: We would never command them to worship us while we are worshiping You. Al-Baghawi: 3/326.\nIn light of this verse, explain the disownment of Allah’s allies from what ignorant people do at their gravesites.\nوَجَعَلۡنَا بَعۡضَكُمۡ لِبَعۡضٖ فِتۡنَةً أَتَصۡبِرُونَۗ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ بَصِيرٗا ٢٠\n(And We have made some of you as a trial for others), a test; the rich are a test for the poor. The poor would say: Why could not I be like him? A healthy person is a test for the sick; a person from a noble family is a test for another of humble social status. Ibn Abbas (k) said: \"It means: I have some of you as a test for others so that you endure patiently what you hear from them.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/326.\nHow do people become a test for one another?\nwords\nوَزَفِيرًاIntense roaring due to its wrath\nمُقَرَّنِينَTheir hands are bound in chains to their necks\nثُبُورًاDestruction, death\nبُورًاDoomed people\nصَرفًاAvert punishment\nفِتنَةًA trial, a test"],[362,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nAsk Allah, the Almighty, to accept your good deeds.\nIf you have a bad companion, then, leave him before you regret his companionship; look for a good one instead, and supplicate Allah to make it easy for you to find.\nDedicate time for reading the Quran daily.\nguid\nBeware of whatever may nullify your good deeds, such as: Shirk, ostentation, reminders of generosity, or hurtful words.\nAllah has made for every Prophet an enemy from among the criminals, so do not despair nor grieve if you have someone who is hostile toward you, for this is the path of the Prophets.\nThe Book of Allah holds the believer firm upon the truth, no matter how many trials he faces, or how intense they may be.\nrefl\nوَقَدِمۡنَآ إِلَىٰ مَا عَمِلُواْ مِنۡ عَمَلٖ فَجَعَلۡنَٰهُ هَبَآءٗ مَّنثُورًا ٢٣\nIbn Al-Mubarak said: \"These will be the deeds that were not intended for the sake of Allah.\" Mujahid said: \"These will be the deeds that were not accepted by Allah.\"Ibn Taimyah: 5/12.\nPerforming good deeds without being sincere to Allah is risky. Explain\nٱلۡمُلۡكُ يَوۡمَئِذٍ ٱلۡحَقُّ لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِۚ\nSomething that offers reassurance and comfort to the heart is the fact that Allah connected His dominion to His name (the Most Gracious), Whose grace and mercy encompass all things. Allah created man weak, but He honored him in order to perfect His blessing, and shower him with His mercy. They all will be brought to stand before Him in humility, they will be motionless with fear before Him, waiting for judgement to be passed upon them, and waiting to see what will happen to them. But, Allah is more merciful toward them than their parents, or even their own selves, so how do you think He will deal with them? Al-Saadi: 582.\nThe sovereignty on the Day of Resurrection is attributed to Allah's Name, the Most Merciful. What does that indicate?\nوَيَوۡمَ يَعَضُّ ٱلظَّالِمُ عَلَىٰ يَدَيۡهِ يَقُولُ يَٰلَيۡتَنِي ٱتَّخَذۡتُ مَعَ ٱلرَّسُولِ سَبِيلٗا ٢٧\nWhoever seeks the people's pleasure by Allah's wrath, will not avail him at all against Allah, just like the wrongdoer who will bite on his hands [in regret] saying, (Oh, I wish I had taken a way with the Messenger ` Woe to me! Would that I had not taken so-and-so as a close friend). Ibn Taimyah: 5/12.\nWhoever seeks the people's pleasure by Allah's wrath, they will not avail him at all against Allah. Substantiate that.\nيَٰوَيۡلَتَىٰ لَيۡتَنِي لَمۡ أَتَّخِذۡ فُلَانًا خَلِيلٗا ٢٨ لَّقَدۡ أَضَلَّنِي عَنِ ٱلذِّكۡرِ بَعۡدَ إِذۡ جَآءَنِيۗ وَكَانَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ خَذُولٗا ٢٩\nThis indicates that trusting a close friend is of the essence, and his advice is taken at face value; therefore, one should not place his trust in anyone except when he is certain of being safe from bad advice. Ibn Ashur: 19/14.\nIn view of this verse, explain the importance of advising between close friends.\nلَّقَدۡ أَضَلَّنِي عَنِ ٱلذِّكۡرِ بَعۡدَ إِذۡ جَآءَنِيۗ وَكَانَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ خَذُولٗا ٢٩\nMeaning: By Allah (He led me away from the remembrance), he obscured my sight, and turned me away from the path of the Quran, like which there is no other remembrance. Al-Biqai: 13/375.\nWhat are the signs of a bad companion?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلۡنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِيٍّ عَدُوّٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَۗ وَكَفَىٰ بِرَبِّكَ هَادِيٗا وَنَصِيرٗا ٣١\nIn effect, Allah says to His Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ): Just like you had an enemy from the polytheists of your people, We, similarly, made for every prophet, before you, an enemy from among the polytheists of his people, hence, you are not singled out for that; so be patient, as our Messengers of Firm Resolve were patient before you. Al-Tabari: 19/265.\nFacing trials is a sign of the truthfulness of those who call others to Allah. Explain in view of the verse.\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَوۡلَا نُزِّلَ عَلَيۡهِ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانُ جُمۡلَةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗۚ كَذَٰلِكَ لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهِۦ فُؤَادَكَۖ وَرَتَّلۡنَٰهُ تَرۡتِيلٗا ٣٢\n(In this way so that We may strengthen your heart thereby), this is an answer to them, saying: We have revealed it over stages to strengthen Muhammad’s (ﷺ) heart. Moreover, it came down at different events that entail each part is revealed for a specific reason. Also, the abrogator and abrogated verses in the Quran had to be revealed separately. (And We have revealed it in a gradual manner), separated by intervals over twenty three years. Ibn Juzay: 2/107.\nMention some of the benefits of revealing the Quran over stages.\nwords\nلاَ يَرجُونَ لِقَاءَنَاThey do not believe in the Hereafter\nوَعَتَواThey became extremely insolent\nهَبَاءًA scattered dust\nمَقِيلًاThe finest resting place\nبِالغَمَامِLight white clouds"],[363,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, grant me a good outcome on all of my affairs, and save me from disgrace in this world, and the torment in the Hereafter.\"\nHelp a preacher in his calling others to Allah.\nSeek refuge with Allah from following your desires.\nguid\nTake warning if you witness the demise of oppressors, or places of their destruction, and do not be heedlessly distracted.\nPreachers must take into account the social background of their audiences, so as to communicate with them accordingly.\nPolytheists are patient with their falsehood, so be even more patient with the truth.\nrefl\nوَلَا يَأۡتُونَكَ بِمَثَلٍ إِلَّا جِئۡنَٰكَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَأَحۡسَنَ تَفۡسِيرًا ٣٣\nThis verse indicates that the one who speaks of knowledge, whether he is a scholar of Hadith, a teacher or, a preacher, should follow the example of his Lord in the way He dealt with His Messengers’ affairs. In this manner, the scholar should deal with people’s affairs. Every time an incident occurs or there is a special occasion, he should quote what is appropriate of Quranic verses and prophetic hadiths, and offer exhortation based on that. Al-Saadi: 582-583.\nIn light of this verse, explain some of the wisdom that a preacher and a teacher should have.\nٱلَّذِينَ يُحۡشَرُونَ عَلَىٰ وُجُوهِهِمۡ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ شَرّٞ مَّكَانٗا وَأَضَلُّ سَبِيلٗا ٣٤\n((The ones who are gathered), they will be gathered, vanquished and walking upside-down (on their faces), or dragged to (Hell). This will be a recompense for what they used to do in their worldly life, driven by the devils, without thinking. The Hereafter will be a mirror of everything that is committed in this life. This worldly life is the plantation for the Hereafter, hence, what is done here will be harvested in the hereafter. Anas bin Malik narrated: A man said, \"O Allah's Messenger, those disbelievers who will be gathered on their faces on the Day of Resurrection; how will Allah gather the disbeliever on his face?\" He said, \"Will not the One Who made him walk on his feet in this world be able to make him walk on his face on the Day of Resurrection?\" When Qatadah heard that, he said: “Yes, by the Power of Our Lord!” [Al-Bukhari]. Al-Biqai: 13/382.\nThe requital befits the action. How does the verse point to this meaning?\nوَقَوۡمَ نُوحٖ لَّمَّا كَذَّبُواْ ٱلرُّسُلَ أَغۡرَقۡنَٰهُمۡ وَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ لِلنَّاسِ ءَايَةٗۖ\n(The messengers), even though they had rejected Noah (u) only, denying one Messenger is, in fact, rejecting them all; therefore, the verse states what their action implied in order to rebuke them. Ibn Atiyah: 4/210.\nRejecting all Messengers is attributed to the people of Noah (u), despite rejecting him only. Why?\nوَقَوۡمَ نُوحٖ لَّمَّا كَذَّبُواْ ٱلرُّسُلَ أَغۡرَقۡنَٰهُمۡ وَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ لِلنَّاسِ ءَايَةٗۖ وَأَعۡتَدۡنَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ عَذَابًا أَلِيمٗا ٣٧ وَعَادٗا وَثَمُودَاْ وَأَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلرَّسِّ وَقُرُونَۢا بَيۡنَ ذَٰلِكَ كَثِيرٗا ٣٨ وَكُلّٗا ضَرَبۡنَا لَهُ ٱلۡأَمۡثَٰلَۖ وَكُلّٗا تَبَّرۡنَا تَتۡبِيرٗا ٣٩\nAllah relates that He presented examples [as warnings] to all nations to whom He sent Messengers, and later destroyed. Nevertheless, He had not punished them until after establishing the proof against them. Ibn Taimyah: 5/14.\nWhen do sinners deserve the punishment?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَتَوۡاْ عَلَى ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِ ٱلَّتِيٓ أُمۡطِرَتۡ مَطَرَ ٱلسَّوۡءِۚ أَفَلَمۡ يَكُونُواْ يَرَوۡنَهَاۚ بَلۡ كَانُواْ لَا يَرۡجُونَ نُشُورٗا ٤٠ وَإِذَا رَأَوۡكَ إِن يَتَّخِذُونَكَ إِلَّا هُزُوًا أَهَٰذَا ٱلَّذِي بَعَثَ ٱللَّهُ رَسُولًا ٤١\n(And they have already come upon the town), the pronoun (they) refers to Quraish and other disbelievers. The (town) is the dwelling of the people of Lot (u). (A rain of evil): Stones from the sky. Allah asked them about their sighting of the town since it was on their trading route to the Levant. Then, He states the reason that prevented them from being admonished by seeing the destroyed town is the fact they did not believe in resurrection. Ibn Juzay: 2/108.\nIn light of this verse, explain the reason for not being admonished by signs and events.\nأَرَءَيۡتَ مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَٰهَهُۥ هَوَىٰهُ أَفَأَنتَ تَكُونُ عَلَيۡهِ وَكِيلًا ٤٣\n(Have you seen the one who takes his desire as his god), whatever he admires and sees as good in his own desires, becomes his religion and his way. As Allah says: (Is one whose evil deed is made appealing to him so he deems it good [like one who is rightly guided]? It is Allah who causes to stray whom He wills and guides whom He wills. So, do not let yourself collapse in grief for them) [35:8]. Ibn Kathir: 3/310.\nHow does one worship his desire?\nأَرَءَيۡتَ مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَٰهَهُۥ هَوَىٰهُ أَفَأَنتَ تَكُونُ عَلَيۡهِ وَكِيلًا ٤٣\nMeaning: He is obedient to his desire, hence, it becomes like a god to him. Desires lead to every corruption, because a human soul is a persistent enjoiner of evil. Ibn Atiyah: 4/212.\nWhen can someone be described as a worshiper of his desire?\nwords\nوَأَصحَابَ الرَّسِّPeople of the Well\nوَقُرُونًاNations, generations\nالأَمثَالَArguments, proofs\nتَبَّرنَاWe annihilated\nمَطَرَ السَّوءِDestructive stones from the sky\nكَادَ لَيُضِلُّنَاHe would have almost led us astray from our gods"],[364,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nReflect on the blessing of shade and sunlight, and write down three benefits of them.\nSupplicate Allah to send rain on the land and its inhabitants, and thank Allah whenever you drink water.\nMaintain ties of kinship by visiting or via phone call.\nguid\nDisbelievers are like animals in terms of their awareness of the Hereafter, rather, they are worse.\nAlign your life in accordance to Fitrah; sleep at night and work during the day.\nA preacher must do his utmost to spread the word of Allah and strive in His cause.\nrefl\nأَمۡ تَحۡسَبُ أَنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ يَسۡمَعُونَ أَوۡ يَعۡقِلُونَۚ إِنۡ هُمۡ إِلَّا كَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ بَلۡ هُمۡ أَضَلُّ سَبِيلًا ٤٤\nAllah excluded most, but not all, of them from understanding the hearing and reasoning proofs, since that was the situation of their masses and followers. However, there were some among them who understood and reasoned, but they were dominated by the love for headship, and were too conceited to follow the Prophet (ﷺ), and become in the same class as the weak and slaves of Quraish, such as Ammar and Bilal (j). Ibn Ashur: 19/37.\nAllah did not exclude all the polytheists from understanding the hearing and reasoning proofs. Why?\nأَمۡ تَحۡسَبُ أَنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ يَسۡمَعُونَ أَوۡ يَعۡقِلُونَۚ إِنۡ هُمۡ إِلَّا كَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ بَلۡ هُمۡ أَضَلُّ سَبِيلًا ٤٤\nMeaning: Because they are not deterred by what they hear while livestock are; they do not show gratitude to the Benevolent (Allah) while He is their guardian, they do not avoid the evildoer while he is their enemy, and they neither hope for reward nor fear punishment since We covered the light of their minds with the shades of the mountains of their misguidance. Had they accepted the faith, these veils would have been removed, and the light of the faith would have shined, hence they would have seen the unique meanings, and grasped the hidden knowledge. (Indeed, those who have believed and done righteous deeds - their Lord will guide them because of their faith) [10:9]. Al-Biqai: 13/395.\nThe disbelievers are more astray than livestock. Why?\nإِنۡ هُمۡ إِلَّا كَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ بَلۡ هُمۡ أَضَلُّ سَبِيلًا ٤٤\nIndeed, they are more astray than livestock, because the herdsman guides the livestock, so they are guided, and they recognize the path that may lead to their doom, so they avoid it, and their fate is better than the fate of these people. Al-Saadi: 584.\nThe livestock are more guided than the disbelievers. Why?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ كَيۡفَ مَدَّ ٱلظِّلَّ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ لَجَعَلَهُۥ سَاكِنٗا ثُمَّ جَعَلۡنَا ٱلشَّمۡسَ عَلَيۡهِ دَلِيلٗا ٤٥\nThere is a blessing in extending and contracting the shade; knowing the times of day for prayers and works, and the blessing of alternating people's benefit between sunlight and shade, where those who are under the sun can cool off under the shade, and those who are in the shade benefit from its contraction. Ibn Ashur: 19/43.\nExplain Allah’s blessing in extending and contracting the shade?\nوَلَوۡ شِئۡنَا لَبَعَثۡنَا فِي كُلِّ قَرۡيَةٖ نَّذِيرٗا ٥١\nMeaning: We have made you a warner to all the worlds, and your rank will be high, so thank Allah for this blessing. Al-Qurtubi: 15/449.\nExplain the wisdom behind making the Prophet (ﷺ) a warner to all the worlds.\nفَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَجَٰهِدۡهُم بِهِۦ جِهَادٗا كَبِيرٗا ٥٢\nThis verse is quoted as evidence of the importance of scholars' strive against the enemies of religion through presenting arguments in defense of the religion, and the leading among them are those who strive against the disbelievers with the Quran. Al-Alusi: 10/33.\nHow can someone strive with the Quran?\nوَيَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَنفَعُهُمۡ وَلَا يَضُرُّهُمۡۗ وَكَانَ ٱلۡكَافِرُ عَلَىٰ رَبِّهِۦ ظَهِيرٗا ٥٥\nIn this verse, the negation of both benefit and harm done by these idols points to the false claims of polytheists who worshiped them. The reason for worship is either hoping for benefit, or averting harm, and both are lacking in these idols by observation. Ibn Ashur: 19/56.\nWorshiping gravesites and shrines is prohibited. Why?\nwords\nمَرَجَHe merges\nفُرَاتٌFresh, palatable\nأُجَاجٌSalty, bitter\nبَرزَخًاA barrier\nوَحِجرًا مَحجُورًاA complete partition\nظَهِيرًاAn assistant to satan against his Lord"],[365,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nFollow the example of the Prophet (ﷺ), and call a disobedient or heedless person to Allah, staring with glad tidings before warning.\nPray during nighttime.\nWhen spending your money, today, on yourself and family, ensure to do it without waste or stinginess.\nguid\nThe preacher should try to abstain from taking money from those whom he preached, or accept any reward from them, as this brings him closer to Allah, and is a sign of his sincerity.\nDo not rely on anyone other than Allah, for he will die, but rely upon Allah, for He is the Ever-Living who never dies.\nBe modest with Allah, the Almighty, wherever you are, for He knows all your sins.\nrefl\nقُلۡ مَآ أَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ مِنۡ أَجۡرٍ إِلَّا مَن شَآءَ أَن يَتَّخِذَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِۦ سَبِيلٗا ٥٧\n(I do not ask you), for conveying glad tidings and warning (for any reward for it), lest you accuse me of calling you for it, or you say: \"Why is not a treasure presented to him from heaven, so he becomes rich?\" It is like he is saying: Abstaining from pursuing great wealth is disliked for one who is asking others, and since that was not my way before Prophethood, how about after I became a Prophet? My only aim is to benefit you. Al-Biqai: 13/412.\nWhat is the sign of truthful preachers who follow the example of Prophets?\nوَتَوَكَّلۡ عَلَى ٱلۡحَيِّ ٱلَّذِي لَا يَمُوتُ وَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِهِۦۚ وَكَفَىٰ بِهِۦ بِذُنُوبِ عِبَادِهِۦ خَبِيرًا ٥٨\nThis verse indicates that a person with perfect faith does not rely upon anyone but Allah, since relying upon other living beings, who are subject to death, despite its temporary benefit, does not last. Ibn Ashur: 19/59.\nReliance upon anyone other than Allah is of no benefit. Explain.\nوَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمُ ٱسۡجُدُواْۤ لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ قَالُواْ وَمَا ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ أَنَسۡجُدُ لِمَا تَأۡمُرُنَا وَزَادَهُمۡ نُفُورٗا۩ ٦٠\nWhen mentioning their refusal to prostrate to the Most Merciful, it is recommended to do the opposite, so, after reciting this verse, the Prophet (ﷺ) prostrated in order to show by action his disparity with what they said. Ibn Ashur: 19/63.\nAfter reciting this verse, it is recommended to prostrate. Why?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ ٱلَّيۡلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَ خِلۡفَةٗ لِّمَنۡ أَرَادَ أَن يَذَّكَّرَ أَوۡ أَرَادَ شُكُورٗا ٦٢\nMoreover, people's moods alter and change throughout the hours of the night and day. So, they may feel energetic or feel tired, be mindful or be heedless, sometimes under stress and sometimes at ease, sometimes focusing in worship and sometimes distracted. So, Allah has caused night and day to come consecutively to people, over and over again, so as to create in them mindfulness, energy, and gratitude toward Him at other times. Al-Saadi: 586.\nThe alternation of the night and the day is a reason for giving thanks to Allah. How?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ ٱلَّيۡلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَ خِلۡفَةٗ لِّمَنۡ أَرَادَ أَن يَذَّكَّرَ أَوۡ أَرَادَ شُكُورٗا ٦٢\nOmar bin Al-Khattab, Alhasan, and Ibn Abbas said: \"Whoever desires to remember what he missed of doing good, praying, etc. in one of them so that he makes it up in the other.\" Ibn Atiyah: 4/218.\nIn light of this verse, explain the effect of the succession of night and day on the servant's worship.\nوَعِبَادُ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَمۡشُونَ عَلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ هَوۡنٗا\nHumbleness comes from their tranquility and dignity. In the interpretation of this verse: They walk on earth with modesty and forbearance; their dignified style and easiness are Prophetic traits. Al-Qurtubi: 15/466.\nDescribe how the believer walks on earth.\nوَإِذَا خَاطَبَهُمُ ٱلۡجَٰهِلُونَ قَالُواْ سَلَٰمٗا ٦٣\nMeaning: When those who are ignorant about Allah address them by what they dislike, they answer them with good words and sound speech. Al-Tabari: 19/295.\nWhat is the wise response to ignorant people?\nwords\nاستَوَى عَلىHe rose high in a manner that suits His Majesty\nنُفُورًاTurning away\nبُرُوجًاGreat stars, constellations\nخِلفَةًIn succession\nهَونًاHumbly\nيَقتُرُواThey are stringent in spending\nقَوَامًاModerate"],[366,"§Al-Furqan\ndeeds\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him as many as a hundred times today.\nFast a day for the sake of Allah, or give charity to someone in need.\nAsk Allah, the Almighty, for the joy of a righteous offsprings and a blessed wife, and let this be among your permanent supplications.\nguid\nUplift your drive, and supplicate Allah to make a good example for the righteous.\nMake the fear of Allah a barrier against polytheism and major sins, and remember the negative effects of sins on your religion and your world.\nReflect on the great mercy and bounty of Allah, the Almighty, as He change the evil deeds of His repentant servant into good deeds.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَدۡعُونَ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَٰهًا ءَاخَرَ وَلَا يَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلنَّفۡسَ ٱلَّتِي حَرَّمَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَّا بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَلَا يَزۡنُونَۚ وَمَن يَفۡعَلۡ ذَٰلِكَ يَلۡقَ أَثَامٗا ٦٨\nThe gravest of the major sins are three: Disbelief, killing a soul unjustly, and committing adultery, as put in order by Allah. In Sahih Al-Bukhari and Muslim, Abdulla bin Masoud said: I said: \"O Allah’s Messenger, what is the greatest sin in the sight of Allah?\" He said, \"That you set up a rival unto Allah though He Alone created you.\" I said, \"What is next?\" He said, \"To kill your son lest he should share your food with you.\" I asked, \"What is next?\" He said, \"To commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.\" The order of these sins reflects the human powers: The mind, the rage, and the lustful desire. Ibn Taimyah: 5/21-22.\nIn this verse, major sins are ordered as follows: Shirk, killing, and adultery. Why?\nإِلَّا مَن تَابَ وَءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ عَمَلٗا صَٰلِحٗا فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يُبَدِّلُ ٱللَّهُ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمۡ حَسَنَٰتٖۗ\nThrough sincere repentance, all past sins are changed into good deeds, because every time the sinner remembers his sin, he regrets it and says, “We belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return,” then, asks for Allah’s forgiveness. Therefore, in this sense, the sin turns into an act of obedience, and on the Day of Resurrection, his sin will not harm him, despite being recorded, because it will be turned into a good deed. Ibn Kathir: 3/316.\nIn light of this verse, explain the great virtue of sincere repentance.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَشۡهَدُونَ ٱلزُّورَ وَإِذَا مَرُّواْ بِٱللَّغۡوِ مَرُّواْ كِرَامٗا ٧٢\n(Those who do not witness falsehood), they do not give false testimony [lying], which means testifying. It is said that it means they do not attend the places of falsehood and distraction, which means witnessing, but the first meaning is more likely. (And when they pass by futility), futility is ill speech. (They pass by with dignity), they turn away from it, and do not associate with those who are engaged in ill speech. Ibn Juzay: 2/113.\nWhat is the duty of a Muslim when he passes by a gathering in which a sin or ill speech is perpetrated?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِّرُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِمۡ لَمۡ يَخِرُّواْ عَلَيۡهَا صُمّٗا وَعُمۡيَانٗا ٧٣\n(They do not fall upon them deaf and blind), they did not turn away from the verses of Allah, rather, they turn to them with their hearings and hearts. Ibn Juzay: 2/113.\nWhat traits should the Muslim display when hearing the verses of the Quran?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا هَبۡ لَنَا مِنۡ أَزۡوَٰجِنَا وَذُرِّيَّٰتِنَا قُرَّةَ أَعۡيُنٖ\nThey call upon Allah with the most perfect of supplications, from which they and those who are connected to them benefit, as do the Muslims at large, such as praying that their spouses and offspring will be righteous. This implies that they strive to teach them, exhort them and advise them, because the one who is keen to attain something and prays to Allah for it, should take measures to attain it. Al-Saadi: 588.\nThe supplication for a righteous wife and offspring entails a duty. What is it?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا هَبۡ لَنَا مِنۡ أَزۡوَٰجِنَا وَذُرِّيَّٰتِنَا قُرَّةَ أَعۡيُنٖ\nAl-Qarthi said: \"There is nothing more comforting to the believer's eyes than seeing his wife and children obedient to Allah, the Almighty.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/347.\nWhat is the most comforting thing to the believer’s eyes?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يُجۡزَوۡنَ ٱلۡغُرۡفَةَ بِمَا صَبَرُواْ وَيُلَقَّوۡنَ فِيهَا تَحِيَّةٗ وَسَلَٰمًا ٧٥ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَاۚ حَسُنَتۡ مُسۡتَقَرّٗا وَمُقَامٗا ٧٦\nThese are eleven attributes: Modesty, forbearance, praying during nighttime, fearing Allah, avoiding spending wastefully, avoiding spending stingily, avoiding shirk, avoiding adultery, avoiding killing a human soul, repenting, avoiding speaking untruthfully, forgiving the offender, accepting the call of truth, and showing one’s need of Allah through invocation. Ibn Ashur: 19/84.\nList the attributes of the servants of the Most Merciful from previous verses, and strive to attain them.\nwords\nمَتَابًاA sincere return to Allah\nلَم يَخِرُّواThey do not prostrate heedlessly, but in obedience\nقُرَّةَ أَعيُنٍA source of happiness\nمَا يَعبَأُHe would not care at all about you\nلِزَامًاA permanent punishment"],[367,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nAttend an Islamic study and Thikr session today.\nGo to a farm or a shop that sells vegetables and fruits and reflect on the manifestations of Allah's greatness in the variety and diversity of the crops.\nForbid a wrong that you seen done by one of your collogues or neighbors in an appropriate manner.\nguid\nAffirming the inimitability of the Quran, since it is made up of these alphabets, yet no one is able to produce something similar to it.\nDisclosing the distress and sorrow that afflicted the Prophet (ﷺ) because of the denial of his people.\nWarning against the consequences of denying Allah's verses, and neglecting them.\nrefl\nوَمَا يَأۡتِيهِم مِّن ذِكۡرٖ مِّنَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ مُحۡدَثٍ إِلَّا كَانُواْ عَنۡهُ مُعۡرِضِينَ ٥\nMentioning Allah's Name, the Most Merciful, to indicate the hideousness of their rejection of whatever comes from His Majesty, the Almighty. Their rejection of what comes to them out of Allah’s mercy for their own benefit is even more hideous. Whenever a reminder, an admonition, or verses from the Quran were revealed by Him, the Almighty, from His mercy, and in accordance with wisdom and benefit, they would renew their rejection and continue on their ways. Al-Alusi: 10/61.\nWhat is the indication of mentioning Allah's Name, the Most Merciful, in this verse?\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ إِلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ كَمۡ أَنۢبَتۡنَا فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ زَوۡجٖ كَرِيمٍ ٧\n(From every noble kind), from every type of plants; this includes sustenance, fruits, and pasture. It is described as (noble) due to its beauty and benefits. Ibn Juzay: 2/114.\nAllah described the plants as (noble), why?\nوَإِذۡ نَادَىٰ رَبُّكَ مُوسَىٰٓ\nAllah returns to the story of Moses (u), which is repeated in the Quran in a way that is not done with other stories, because it contains important wisdom and lessons. In this story, Allah tells us how Moses dealt with the wrongdoers and the believers, and how he was the bringer of a great law, the bringer of the Torah, which is the best of the divinely revealed Books after the Quran. Al-Saadi: 589.\nMoses' story is repeated in the Quran more than any other story. Why?\nوَإِذۡ نَادَىٰ رَبُّكَ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنِ ٱئۡتِ ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٠ قَوۡمَ فِرۡعَوۡنَۚ أَلَا يَتَّقُونَ ١١\nThere are different types of wrongdoings: They wronged themselves by worshiping things that are unworthy of worship. They wronged others by denying their rights, where they enslaved the Children of Israel and persecuted them. Ibn Ashur: 19/104.\nWhat are types of wrongdoings committed by the people of Pharaoh?\nقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ ١٢ وَيَضِيقُ صَدۡرِي وَلَا يَنطَلِقُ لِسَانِي فَأَرۡسِلۡ إِلَىٰ هَٰرُونَ ١٣ وَلَهُمۡ عَلَيَّ ذَنۢبٞ فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقۡتُلُونِ ١٤\nMoses asked Allah to remove these difficulties for him, as he said in Surat Ta-Ha: (My Lord, reassure my heart for me ` And ease my task for me ` And untie the knot from my tongue ` That they may understand my speech ` And appoint for me a helper from my family ` Aaron, my brother ` Increase my strength through him ` And let him share my task ` That we may exalt You much ` And remember You much ` For indeed You are All-Watchful over us) [20:25-36]. Ibn Kathir: 3/321.\nWhat is the aim of Moses' supplication?\nوَيَضِيقُ صَدۡرِي وَلَا يَنطَلِقُ لِسَانِي فَأَرۡسِلۡ إِلَىٰ هَٰرُونَ ١٣\nThis proves that whoever takes a task seriously, and fears his shortcomings, there is no blame on him to choose someone to help him achieve the task. Al-Qurtubi: 16/13.\nWhat do we learn from Moses' request to have his brother Aaron as a helper?\nوَلَهُمۡ عَلَيَّ ذَنۢبٞ فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقۡتُلُونِ ١٤ قَالَ كَلَّاۖ\nMeaning: They will not be able to kill you, hence, Pharaoh was not able to kill Moses, even though Moses opposed him and stood up to him, and regarded his views as foolish and him and his people as misguided. Al-Saadi: 589.\nPharaoh could not harm Moses. Why?\nwords\nبَاخِعٌYou would kill yourself with grief\nمُحدَثٍA recent revelation\nزَوجٍ كَرِيمٍA beautiful and useful kind"],[368,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You to grant me fear of You in private and in public, and I ask You for the word of truth in times of contentment and anger.\"\nLook for the weak and oppressed, and defend them in pursuit of the divine reward.\nReflect on three signs of the greatness of Allah, the Almighty.\nguid\nNatural fear does not contradict the fear of Allah, the Almighty.\nWhen arrogant and lofty people lose an argument, they resort to threat, intimidation, and the use of force.\nPreachers must practice the debate, and how to establish clear, solid arguments, as this is more conducive to the emergence of the truth.\nrefl\nوَتِلۡكَ نِعۡمَةٞ تَمُنُّهَا عَلَيَّ أَنۡ عَبَّدتَّ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ ٢٢\nMeaning: You remind me of raising me, while you forget your crime against the Children of Israel by enslaving and mistreating them. Or, he meant to say: How can you remind me of raising me, while you enslaved my people? Whomever his people are insulted, would be a humiliated person, hence, your enslavement of the Children of Israel nullified your benevolence to me. Al-Baghawi: 3/356.\nExplain Moses' response to Pharaoh when he reminded him of his benevolence to him.\nقَالَ إِنَّ رَسُولَكُمُ ٱلَّذِيٓ أُرۡسِلَ إِلَيۡكُمۡ لَمَجۡنُونٞ ٢٧ قَالَ رَبُّ ٱلۡمَشۡرِقِ وَٱلۡمَغۡرِبِ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَآۖ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٨\n(If only you had sense), in that there is an implicit indication that what you accused Moses of, namely insanity, is, in fact, present in you, for you accused the smartest, most rational and most knowledgeable person of being insane, when, in fact, you are the insane ones because you denied the Being Whose existence is the most obvious, namely the Creator of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them. Al-Saadi: 590.\nIn Moses' words, there is a response to Pharaoh's accusation of insanity. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَ رَبُّ ٱلۡمَشۡرِقِ وَٱلۡمَغۡرِبِ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَآۖ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٨\nIn the beginning, Moses (u) used a soft approach in calling Pharaoh to Allah, but due to Pharaoh’s impolite last response to him, Moses ended this proof by saying: (If only you had sense), which means that you already know that. Hence, Moses' response was sharp, yet gentle, and clear, yet implied. Al-Biqai: 14/27.\nIt is wise to the right words at the right time. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَ رَبُّ ٱلۡمَشۡرِقِ وَٱلۡمَغۡرِبِ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَآۖ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٨\nOne may wonder about Moses' responses; he started by saying: (If only you had sure faith), then he said: (If only you had sense)? The explanation is that, in the beginning, Moses was lenient in addressing them in hope that they would accept the faith, but after he witnessed their stubbornness and falsification, he rebuked them by saying: (If only you had sense), which was in response to Pharaoh's saying: (Your messenger who has been sent to you is truly insane). Ibn Juzay: 2/117.\nAt the start, Moses said to Pharaoh: (If only you had sure faith), then, later he said: (If only you had sense). Why?\nقَالَ لَئِنِ ٱتَّخَذۡتَ إِلَٰهًا غَيۡرِي لَأَجۡعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلۡمَسۡجُونِينَ ٢٩\nMoses asked Allah to When proof had been established against Pharaoh, clearly and rationally, he resorted to using his force and authority against Moses. Ibn Kathir: 3/322.\nHow do wrongdoers behave when they lose an argument?\nفَأَلۡقَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ ثُعۡبَانٞ مُّبِينٞ ٣٢\n(Manifest), this indicates that it was a real serpent, without ambiguity or imagination. Ibn Ashur: 19/123.\nWhat is the benefit of describing the serpent as manifest?\nقَالُوٓاْ أَرۡجِهۡ وَأَخَاهُ وَٱبۡعَثۡ فِي ٱلۡمَدَآئِنِ حَٰشِرِينَ ٣٦ يَأۡتُوكَ بِكُلِّ سَحَّارٍ عَلِيمٖ ٣٧ فَجُمِعَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ لِمِيقَٰتِ يَوۡمٖ مَّعۡلُومٖ ٣٨ وَقِيلَ لِلنَّاسِ هَلۡ أَنتُم مُّجۡتَمِعُونَ ٣٩\nThis was what Allah decreed would happen to them, so that all the people would gather in one place and the signs and proof of Allah would be made manifest before them all in one day. Ibn Kathir: 3/322.\nPharaoh tried to nullify Moses' argument by gathering the magicians, but the opposite happened. Explain.\nwords\nالضَّآلِّينَAmong the ignorant, before the revelation\nحُكمًاProphethood\nعَبَّدتَYou enslaved them\nوَنَزَعَ يَدَهُHe drew out his hand\nأَرجِهLet him wait\nحَاشِرِينَSoldiers who gather the magicians"],[369,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nPerform a Da'wah-related act, and patiently endure the toil and trouble in pursuit of divine reward.\nSupplicate Allah, the Almighty, to forgive your sins, and keep firm your faith.\nWrite down the places where Allah, the Almighty, protected, supported and helped His Prophet Moses (u) in this noble surah.\nguid\nWhoever seeks honor and power outside the religion of Allah, Allah will humiliate him.\nThe threats of tyrants toward the righteous are means of reaching higher ranks by the righteous in this world and in the Hereafter.\nPeople become very insignificant in the sight of Allah when they disobey Him Pharaoh was an insolent king claiming Lordship, and the next thing he was drowned in the sea.\nrefl\nقَالَ لَهُم مُّوسَىٰٓ أَلۡقُواْ مَآ أَنتُم مُّلۡقُونَ ٤٣\nMoses did not throw his staff first because he was not in a war setting where one side would benefit from attacking first, rather, this was a debate setting, where it was better to let the opponent present his arguments, then it would be easier to refute them, hence, the truth would come out and falsehood would be defeated. This approach, followed by Moses, was inspired by his Lord. Al-Jaza'iri: 3/649.\nMoses did not throw his staff first. Why?\nفَأَلۡقَوۡاْ حِبَالَهُمۡ وَعِصِيَّهُمۡ وَقَالُواْ بِعِزَّةِ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِنَّا لَنَحۡنُ ٱلۡغَٰلِبُونَ ٤٤\n((And they said), they swore (by the might of Pharaoh). Whoever swears by anything other than Allah -as saying: By the life of so and so, etc.- is a follower of this ignorance. Al-Biqai: 14/32-33.\nSwearing by something is equating it with Allah in veneration. Explain.\nفَأَلۡقَوۡاْ حِبَالَهُمۡ وَعِصِيَّهُمۡ وَقَالُواْ بِعِزَّةِ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِنَّا لَنَحۡنُ ٱلۡغَٰلِبُونَ ٤٤\nThey said that in order to frighten Moses, and weaken his resolve when he would throw his staff since they knew that a magician’s determination was one of the biggest reasons for his success and his impact on the spectators. Ibn Ashur: 19/127.\nThe magicians said (it is we who will be the victorious). Why?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَكَبِيرُكُمُ ٱلَّذِي عَلَّمَكُمُ ٱلسِّحۡرَ\nThis is stubborn talk, and anyone can see that it is nonsense, for they had never met Moses before that day, so, how could he have been their chief who taught them how to do magic. No rational person would say this. Ibn Kathir: 3/324.\nThis verse indicates the stubbornness of Pharaoh. Explain.\nقَالُواْ لَا ضَيۡرَۖ\nBut the magicians said, when they had tasted the sweetness of faith: (No harm), we do not care what you threaten us with. Al-Saadi: 592.\nThe magicians did not care about Pharaoh’s threats. Why?\nإِنَّا نَطۡمَعُ أَن يَغۡفِرَ لَنَا رَبُّنَا خَطَٰيَٰنَآ أَن كُنَّآ أَوَّلَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٥١\nThey expressed hope to indicate that all causes of happiness come from Allah only. Al-Biqai: 14/36.\nWhat does expressing hope in Allah’s forgiveness indicate?\nوَإِنَّا لَجَمِيعٌ حَٰذِرُونَ ٥٦\nMeaning: Being cautious was one of his traits and habits, therefore, the community must join him in that too, which means that it is our habit to be cautious of ongoing events, and what dire consequences they could have. This is a great principle in governance, which is blocking the means of corruption, even if their probable lead to corruption is weak. Ibn Ashur: 19/131.\nThis verse indicates a great principle in governance. Explain.\nwords\nبِعِزَّةِ فِرعَونَThey swore by Pharaoh's might and power\nتَلقَفُDevours quickly\nمَا يَأفِكُونَWhat they falsified\nلاَ ضَيرَNo harm\nمُنقَلِبُونَWe will return\nحَاشِرِينَGatherers of the army\nلَشِرذِمَةٌA small band"],[370,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nUsing a website or a text message, write about the trend of invoking and sacrificing for anyone besides Allah and its risk on individuals and society, then share this information with whoever may benefit from it.\nSay, \"O Allah, grant my body health, O Allah, grant my hearing health, O Allah, grant my sight health. There is none worthy of worship but You.\"\nList three of Allah's blessings upon you, then thank Him for them, as it is one of the reasons to increase your love for Allah, as Allah's close friend (u) said:\nguid\nWhen reflecting on Allah's revelation about the disbelief of most people, you should not feel secure from misguidance, hence, ask Allah often to keep you steadfast in faith.\nBeware of blind imitation of forefathers, which was the reason for the demise of nations, as disbelievers strayed from the path of Allah because of it.\nKnow that if an illness afflicts you, neither Prophets nor allies of Allah can ward it off, except Allah alone, Glory be to Him.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّا تَرَٰٓءَا ٱلۡجَمۡعَانِ قَالَ أَصۡحَٰبُ مُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّا لَمُدۡرَكُونَ ٦١ قَالَ كَلَّآۖ إِنَّ مَعِيَ رَبِّي سَيَهۡدِينِ ٦٢\n(Moses said), rebuking and directing them to the fact that Allah's plan avails of his own plan. (No) they would not overtake you. (My Lord is with me) by protection and help. (He will guide me) soon to your safety and victory over them. Al-Alusi: 10/84.\nFirm faith is a beautiful thing by which Allah keeps the believer steadfast during trials. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَٱتۡلُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ نَبَأَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ ٦٩ إِذۡ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوۡمِهِۦ مَا تَعۡبُدُونَ ٧٠\nMeaning: Recount to the people, O Muhammad (ﷺ), the story of Abraham. What is meant here is this particular aspect in his life, otherwise, there are many stories about him, but one of the most amazing and significant is this story that speaks of his message, his call to his people, and how he argued with them and proved to them that what they were following was false. (When he said to his father and his people, \"What do you worship?\"). Al-Saadi: 592.\nAllah commanded His Prophet (ﷺ) to recount about a particular aspect of Abraham's life, which was calling his people to Allah. Why?\nقَالُواْ بَلۡ وَجَدۡنَآ ءَابَآءَنَا كَذَٰلِكَ يَفۡعَلُونَ ٧٤\nThey gave up on arguing for the ability of their idols to hear, benefit or harm, since all these things are clearly indefensible, and chose instead to rely on the grounds of imitating their fathers. In essence, they were saying: These idols do not hear, benefit, nor harm us, but we found our fathers doing the same thing we are doing, and worshiping them like we do, hence, we followed their example. Al-Alusi: 10/92.\nIs imitating the fathers, in doing wrong, an accepted argument on the Day of Resurrection?\nأَنتُمۡ وَءَابَآؤُكُمُ ٱلۡأَقۡدَمُونَ ٧٦\nDescribing the forefathers as (ancient) emphasizes the apathy of following their example, since it is common for nations to consider following the more ancient traditions as indisputable. Ibn Ashur: 19/141.\nWhy are the forefathers described as “ancient”?\nفَإِنَّهُمۡ عَدُوّٞ لِّيٓ إِلَّا رَبَّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٧٧\nOne may say: How are wood, iron, and copper described as enemies to the son of Adam? The meaning of that is: If I worship them in this life, they will be my enemies on the Day of Resurrection, as Allah says, (They have taken gods other than Allah, in order that they may protect them from punishment ` Never! They will deny their worship and will become their enemies) [19:81-82]. Al-Tabari: 19/363.\nDespite being inanimate objects, the idols are described as enemies of the son of Adam. Why?\nٱلَّذِي خَلَقَنِي فَهُوَ يَهۡدِينِ ٧٨ وَٱلَّذِي هُوَ يُطۡعِمُنِي وَيَسۡقِينِ ٧٩ وَإِذَا مَرِضۡتُ فَهُوَ يَشۡفِينِ ٨٠ وَٱلَّذِي يُمِيتُنِي ثُمَّ يُحۡيِينِ ٨١ وَٱلَّذِيٓ أَطۡمَعُ أَن يَغۡفِرَ لِي خَطِيٓـَٔتِي يَوۡمَ ٱلدِّينِ ٨٢\nMy Lord is the One Who has my benefit and harm, the All-Capable, the All-Sovereign, and to Him belongs this worldly life and the Hereafter. My Lord is not one who when is called does not hear, nor could benefit, or harm. This talk from Abraham was an argument before his people to explain that deity and submission must be only to the One Who has these powers; not to useless harmless objects. Al-Tabari: 19/363.\nWhat are the rational proofs, mentioned by Abraham, for the Lordship of Allah, and falsehood of others?\nوَإِذَا مَرِضۡتُ فَهُوَ يَشۡفِينِ ٨٠\nHe attributed illness to himself, and attributed cure to Allah, out of veneration of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/119.\nThis verse shows an etiquette of how should believers deal with Allah. What is it?\nwords\nتَرَاءَىWhen the two groups saw one another\nفِرقٍA part of the sea\nكَالطَّودِLike a mountain\nوَأَزلَفنَا ثَمَّWe brought thereto, Pharaoh and his people"],[371,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to forgive your parents and have mercy on them.\nBefriend those whom their friendship brings you closer to Allah.\nTeach a Muslim a Surah from the Holy Quran, for the sake of Allah.\nguid\nBe mindful of your heart, and keep it pure and sound, as only those come to Allah with sound hearts will be saved.\nBeware of the path of the deviators who misguide people, as Allah made Hellfire their abode.\nEnsure to have righteous friends, for they may benefit you with intercession, Allah's willing.\nrefl\nوَٱجۡعَل لِّي لِسَانَ صِدۡقٖ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرِينَ ٨٤\n(An honorable mention among the later generations), praised and ever-honored, as most interpreters said. Ibn Atiyah: 4/235.\nWhat is meant by: (An honorable mention among the later generations)?\nيَوۡمَ لَا يَنفَعُ مَالٞ وَلَا بَنُونَ ٨٨ إِلَّا مَنۡ أَتَى ٱللَّهَ بِقَلۡبٖ سَلِيمٖ ٨٩\nThis means that wealth will only benefit those who spent it for the sake of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/119.\nWhen will wealth be beneficial on the Day of Resurrection?\nإِلَّا مَنۡ أَتَى ٱللَّهَ بِقَلۡبٖ سَلِيمٖ ٨٩\nThe heart is singled out for mention because if it is healthy, the whole body is healthy, and if it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Al-Qurtubi: 16/44.\nThe heart is singled out for mention. Why?\nوَجُنُودُ إِبۡلِيسَ أَجۡمَعُونَ ٩٥\n(And the soldiers of Iblees), his descendants, and everyone following him, since they become his soldiers and helpers. Ibn Atiyah: 4/236.\nWhen does man become one of the soldiers of Iblees?\nفَمَا لَنَا مِن شَٰفِعِينَ ١٠٠ وَلَا صَدِيقٍ حَمِيمٖ ١٠١\nQatadah said: They will know for sure that a righteous friend will benefit them, and a close friend will intercede for them. Ibn Kathir: 3/329.\nHow does this verse exhort people to have righteous friends?\nإِذۡ قَالَ لَهُمۡ أَخُوهُمۡ نُوحٌ\n(When their brother) in kinship, (Noah said to them), Allah sent the Messengers from the same tribe or clan as that to whom He sent them, lest they be reluctant to submit to him, and because they would know his real character, so they would not need to ask and find out about him. Al-Saadi: 594.\nAllah sent the Messengers from the same tribe or clan of their people. Why?\nقَالُوٓاْ أَنُؤۡمِنُ لَكَ وَٱتَّبَعَكَ ٱلۡأَرۡذَلُونَ ١١١\nThus, it is clear that they were too arrogant to accept the truth and they were ignorant of the real facts. If their aim had been to find out the truth, they would have said, if they had any confusion or doubt about his message: Prove to us the validity of the message that you have brought by means of valid arguments and proofs. Al-Saadi: 594.\nThis verse shows that they were too arrogant to follow the truth. How?\nwords\nلِسَانَA good praise\nالآخِرينThose who come after me until the Last Day\nسَلِيمٍA heart. free of shirk, hypocrisy and hatred\nوَأُزلِفَتِIt will be brought closer\nوَبُرِّزَتِIt will be uncovered\nفَكُبكِبُواThey will be gathered and hurled into Hell\nحَمِيمٍA close, compassionate friend\nكَرَّةًA chance to return back to worldly life\nالأَرذَلُونَThe lowest class of people"],[372,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nGo to weak and poor righteous people, sit with them, and gift them.\nSupplicate Allah to destroy the wrongdoers at the hands of other wrongdoers, and bring out the Muslims from among them safe.\nListen to an admonishment and implement what you heard.\nguid\nWhen wrongdoers and tyrants lose an argument, they resort to force.\nWhen transgression become very intense, it is ordained to ask Allah for judgment.\nAllah's rapid answer to Noah, because he endured patiently for a long time.\nrefl\nقَالَ وَمَا عِلۡمِي بِمَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١١٢\nNoah said to his people: How would I know what my followers are doing? I care only about their outward behavior, and I am not commanded to search for their private deeds. Therefore, whoever shows good deeds, I would think positively of him, and whoever shows bad deeds, I would think negatively of him. He says: The reckoning for their private deeds is only with my Lord if you realize, because He knows their private and public deeds. Al-Tabari: 19/370.\nThe preacher is not responsible for people's private deeds. Explain in view of this verse.\nوَمَآ أَنَا۠ بِطَارِدِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١١٤ إِنۡ أَنَا۠ إِلَّا نَذِيرٞ مُّبِينٞ ١١٥\nThey demanded from him to drive away the weak and poor people, just like Quraish did. (I am only a clear warner), Allah has not sent me to the rich people only, I am only a Messenger, conveying to you the message I was sent with. Therefore, whoever obeyed me, would be the winner with Allah, even if he was poor. Al-Qurtubi: 16/53.\nIs the Prophets' message exclusive to the rich?\nأَتَبۡنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةٗ تَعۡبَثُونَ ١٢٨\nThe phase of admonishment is wider than that of changing the wrong. Hence, Hūd's (u) admonishment was directed to the sicknesses in their souls, and it contained no direction to change what they had built of landmarks and palaces. Ibn Ashur: 19/166.\nDid Hūd (u) denounce his people for erecting buildings?\nأَتَبۡنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةٗ تَعۡبَثُونَ ١٢٨ وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَخۡلُدُونَ ١٢٩ وَإِذَا بَطَشۡتُم بَطَشۡتُمۡ جَبَّارِينَ ١٣٠\nProphet Hūd's (u) rebuke to his people indicates that their hearts were overwhelmed with love for this worldly life and arrogance until it drew them away from submission to Allah. Al-Alusi: 10/108.\nWhat is the consequence of an exaggerated love for worldly life?\nأَمَدَّكُم بِأَنۡعَٰمٖ وَبَنِينَ ١٣٣\nIn counting the blessings, the mention of livestock came first because it was the biggest blessing for those who lived there at the time. From livestock, they get their food, clothing, and means for travel. Ibn Ashur: 19/170.\nIn this verse, the mention of livestock comes first. Why?\nقَالُواْ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيۡنَآ أَوَعَظۡتَ أَمۡ لَمۡ تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡوَٰعِظِينَ ١٣٦\nThe people of Aad had reached a great level of power and control over the land, which led them to say, (Who is more powerful than us) [41:15]. A long period of time passed over them, and through which they pursued their desires and lusts and became intensely boastful. They neglected the important aspect for humans, which is the religion and the purity of the soul. They made light of their obligations toward Allah and ridiculed those who advised them. Ibn Ashur: 19/165.\nExplain the risk of the abundance of blessings on a community that is heedless of the remembrance of Allah.\nقَالُواْ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيۡنَآ أَوَعَظۡتَ أَمۡ لَمۡ تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡوَٰعِظِينَ ١٣٦\n(They said, \"It is the same to us whether you admonish us or not\"), we are indifferent to what you say; we do not hear, nor care about what you say. Al-Qurtubi: 16/59.\nExplain the situation of those with hardened hearts when they are admonished and reminded of Allah, the Almighty.\nwords\nالمَرجُومِينَThose who are stoned to death\nفَافتَحSo, Judge\nالمَشحُونِFull of people, animals, and things\nرِيعٍA higher ground\nآيَةًA landmark\nتَعبَثُونَOverlooking and mocking those who pass by\nمَصَانِعَFortified palaces and great fortresses\nأَمَدَّكُمHe who provided you\nسَوَاءٌ عَلَينَاIt is all the same to us"],[373,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nShare a text message in which you explain that preachers who call others to Allah with sincerity to Him, and do not desire this world, will be successful.\nTeach a Muslim some of the daily Athkar, seeking the reward from Allah.\nWrite a message in which you explain the harm caused by the disbelievers and hypocrites, and aspects of their corruption in the land.\nguid\nDo not care about the disdainful behavior of the deniers and their mocking, as it is the game of the weak and ignorant.\nTrustworthiness is the mark of the Messengers and truthful preachers in all nations and times.\nBeware of obeying the transgressors in committing sins, for the consequences of obeying them will be grave.\nrefl\nفَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَهۡلَكۡنَٰهُمۡۚ\nThe means of their destruction had been described in more than one place in the Quran: Allah sent against them a strong and furious wind, which was a fiercely blowing wind that was intensely cold. Thus, the means of their destruction was suited to their nature, for they were the strongest and fiercest of people, so Allah overpowered them with something that was even stronger and fiercer than them. Ibn Kathir: 3/331.\nIn view of the punishment of Aad, explain this saying: (A befitting recompense).\nكَذَّبَتۡ ثَمُودُ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ١٤١\nThey rejected Salih (u), who brought the message of the Oneness of Allah, to which all the Messengers called people. Therefore, their rejection of him was a rejection of all the Messengers. Al-Saadi: 596.\nHow did Thamud reject all the Messengers?\nوَمَآ أَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ مِنۡ أَجۡرٍۖ إِنۡ أَجۡرِيَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٤٥\nSo that you would might say: What prevents us from following you is the fact that you want to take our wealth (my reward is only with the Lord of the worlds), I only seek reward from Him. Al-Saadi: 596.\nThis verse mentions a sign of truthfulness of allies of Allah. What is it?\nأَتُتۡرَكُونَ فِي مَا هَٰهُنَآ ءَامِنِينَ ١٤٦\n(Will you be left): This is a threat to them, which means: Do you hope to be left in your indulgence in blessings despite your disbelief. Ibn Juzay: 2/121.\nIn a society where blessings and sins are present, do you expect this situation to last?\nأَتُتۡرَكُونَ فِي مَا هَٰهُنَآ ءَامِنِينَ ١٤٦\n(Secure) is a description of their state, which points to the importance of this blessing (security); it is the greatest of all blessings, without which other blessings can never be enjoyed. Ibn Ashur: 19/175.\nThe blessing of security is one of the greatest blessings. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُفۡسِدُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَا يُصۡلِحُونَ ١٥٢\nSince causing corruption does not contradict doing good sometimes, Allah follows this statement: (who cause corruption) by saying, (and never do what is right) in order to show that their corruption was full, and did not had any good in it. Al-Alusi: 10/112.\nWhat is the benefit in combining the causing of corruption with the absence of doing good?\nفَأَخَذَهُمُ ٱلۡعَذَابُۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكۡثَرُهُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٥٨\n(But they hamstrung her and so became regretful), they regretted what they did when they became certain of the punishment, since they were given respite for three days , and with each passing day, they saw a sign indicating their near demise, so they became remorseful when they faced the punishment but to no avail. It is said that regret did not avail them, since they did not repent. Al-Qurtubi: 16/67.\nWhen does regret become unbeneficial to the sinner?\nwords\nخُلُقُA custom, habit\nطَلعُهَا هَضِيمٌLaden with tender fruit\nفَارِهِينَSkilled at carving, insolent and boastful\nالمُسرِفِينَTransgressors\nشِربٌA share of water\nفَعَقَرُوهَاThey slaughtered it"],[374,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, make me hate disbelief, deviance and rebellion.\"\nForbid an evil act, then, share a message in which you explain that if a society slackens in enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong, then, the opposite will spread out, enjoining what is wrong and forbidding what is right.\nWrite few words about the risk and punishment of defrauding others in weight or measure, and pass it around to the sellers in your neighborhood.\nguid\nWhen the heart is devoid of the love of Allah, then, anything can be said about the extinction of human nature.\nThe supplication of the oppressed will be answered, especially if he is righteous.\nWhen evil spreads out and wrongdoing and corruption become excessive, then expect the punishment.\nrefl\nأَتَأۡتُونَ ٱلذُّكۡرَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٦٥\n(Do you approach males), doing so is contrary to all those who belong to worlds that are made up of males and females, since none of them approach males. This warns that this horrible act goes against the nature of everything, even animals do not engage in such an abhorred act. Hence, it was a shameful act of their own invention and was never done by someone else before them. Ibn Ashur: 19/179.\nThe verse explained the abominable nature of the actions of Lot’s people. How?\nقَالُواْ لَئِن لَّمۡ تَنتَهِ يَٰلُوطُ لَتَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمُخۡرَجِينَ ١٦٧\nThey said the like of those who came before them, their hearts resembled each other in disbelief, hence, their words became similar. Al-Saadi: 596.\nWhat is the indication of the similarity of the words of disbelievers in the past and present?\nقَالَ إِنِّي لِعَمَلِكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡقَالِينَ ١٦٨\nLot (u) said: (I am one of those who utterly detest your practice), detesting means abhorring and renouncing. Allah's Prophets are His allies, they like what He likes, and detest what He detests. Ibn Taimyah: 5/49.\nDraw from this verse one of the important traits of Allah's allies.\nرَبِّ نَجِّنِي وَأَهۡلِي مِمَّا يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٦٩\n(My Lord, save me and my family from what they do), save me and my family from the punishment for their actions. Lot (u) supplicated Allah, after he despaired of their faith, that he would not be affected by their punishment. Al-Qurtubi: 16/69.\nExplain the intense fear of Lot (u) from the coming of punishment.\nفَنَجَّيۡنَٰهُ وَأَهۡلَهُۥٓ أَجۡمَعِينَ ١٧٠ إِلَّا عَجُوزٗا فِي ٱلۡغَٰبِرِينَ ١٧١\n(Except an old woman), she was his wife (among) those who (remained behind) in punishment, as We would not save her because of Our past decree, and for the fact that she did not follow him in the religion, but preferred her people. Al-Biqai: 14/83.\nTies of faith are stronger than that of family. Explain in light of this verse.\nإِنِّي لَكُمۡ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٞ ١٧٨ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ١٧٩ وَمَآ أَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ مِنۡ أَجۡرٍۖ إِنۡ أَجۡرِيَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٨٠\nThe message of all these Prophets, as Allah relates about them, followed the same format, since they all concur with enjoining the fear of Allah, obedience to Him, sincerity in worshiping Him, and refraining from accepting a reward for conveying the message. Al-Baghawi: 3/371.\nWhat are the traits that are common to all the Messengers (p) in their preaching?\nأَوۡفُواْ ٱلۡكَيۡلَ وَلَا تَكُونُواْ مِنَ ٱلۡمُخۡسِرِينَ ١٨١ وَزِنُواْ بِٱلۡقِسۡطَاسِ ٱلۡمُسۡتَقِيمِ ١٨٢\nMeaning: A command to give full and complete weight, and forbidding to decrease but not increase. Apparently, increasing the measure and weight is neither enjoined, nor forbidden, which indicates that whoever does it, has done well; and whoever does not, no blame on him. Al-Alusi: 10/117.\nIncreasing the measure and weight is neither enjoined, nor forbidden. What do we learn from that?\nwords\nعَادُونَA transgressing people\nالقَالِينَThose who utterly abhor your deed\nالغَابِرِينَThose who remained in destruction\nأَصحَابُ الأَيكَةِThe companions of the thicket, people of Shu'aib\nالمُخسِرِينَDefrauders\nبِالقِسطَاسِA scale, balance"]])